he prose-and-rows items: P3-γ either seal `state.post` for `post_capture_digest` or reword the bound in all four places it is stated; P3-δ either reword the `N-workspace-cwd` note as defence-in-depth and message-keyed or assert admission properly; P3-ε′ add the orphan-blob leak row to the shipped harness; P3-ζ′ record the duplicated fidelity vocabulary as an explicit bound for the final leaf, or export one owner.\n11|Results must carry a section that names P3-ε closed and P3-ζ / P3-η either closed or deferred to TASK-260830-32ypr2 with the reason, plus the ratio you MEASURE over the seventeen AC rows — not the one you planned.\n12|Procedure: your candidate is on a base that already carries a12d1bd; current origin/main is c3aae73. Do not refresh unless origin/main actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2g5be6` and audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old base> <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keeping README/LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content. You are a MIDDLE leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability — the final leaf carries the registry bindings and the pin. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (30 commands at trunk c3aae73 — read the count from the candidate config rather than assuming it; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs). Update TASK-260830-2g5be6_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and TASK-260830-2g5be6_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-2g5be6 --role developer` so revision 2 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in — this is 