{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":69,"recorded_at":1780531400000133,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b27e-fc16-7480-80cb-258e6ba890ab"},"task_id":"01a0b27e-fc16-7480-80cb-258e6ba890ab","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b27e-fc16-7480-80cb-258e6ba890ab","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2g5be6/TASK-260830-2g5be6_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-2g5be6 (implement-native-capture-and-source-race-check), the SECOND leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q (canonical-session-capture-and-evidence, EPIC M4). Predecessor TASK-260830-24z2b3 is accepted and checkpointed on the Story branch: it landed internal/clonebundle with the closed TYPES and their builders/decoders — BuildRawObjectManifest, BuildCaptureManifest, BuildCanonicalSession/Event, DecodeCaptureBoundary, DecodeStableSnapshotProof, DecodeWorkspaceBinding, DecodeNativeIdentity, DecodeSourceBasis, DecodeSourceEvidence, InstallRawBlob, SanitizeNativeKey, ParseGeneration, CheckDigestsEqual, CheckOrdinalContiguity, RefuseUnstableForTarget, RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete, ValidCaptureClass. The final leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 (projection fidelity: opaque events, foreign reasoning, incomplete tools) follows you and owns the Story-close items. Your leaf is the CAPTURE OPERATION itself over a real on-disk provider store: produce the Raw Object Manifest and Capture Manifest from actual bytes, not from hand-built fixtures. Do NOT fork a second manifest/boundary/blob model — every artifact you emit must be produced through the landed clonebundle builders and validated by the landed decoders, and the results must name which builder each artifact came from.\n2|Scope, all against pinned Sections 13.14.1, 10.2 and 7.8:\n3|(1) A capture walk over a provider store directory that yields sorted unique Raw Object Manifest entries with a sanitized native key (through SanitizeNativeKey), byte count, blob ID and Blob Descriptor ID. Containment is not optional: walk with the landed internal/dirnode openat-relative discipline (a symlinked intermediate component and a FIFO must both refuse before any open of the payload, and the refusal must name the member, not \"open failed\"), and never let a capture escape the store root.\n4|(2) Capture Item classification into the closed class vocabulary durable_payload|durable_index_required|durable_sidecar|derived_cache_optional|credential|machine_auth|runtime_state|transient_lock|unknown, with included items carrying descriptor + count and no reason, excluded items carrying null content fields and a stable reason, credential/machine_auth/runtime_state/transient_lock ALWAYS excluded (a fixture store must contain one of each and the test must prove its bytes never reach a blob, a manifest, a log line or an error string), and `unknown` driving raw_complete=false and blocking maximal-safe through the landed RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete.\n5|(3) Capture Boundary construction from real evidence. `stable` requires a Stable Snapshot Proof with one of closed_store|immutable_snapshot|verified_log_prefix|provider_quiescence, the generation, equal pre/post digests and the input/foreground/background idle facts. Size equality is NEVER proof: ship a fixture whose pre and post bytes differ at equal size and prove the boundary refuses stable. `unstable_archive` carries generation, pre/post digests, source_not_quiescent, the explicit acknowledgement and target_projection_forbidden=true, is core-created for archive-only output, and can never enter a target branch (drive RefuseUnstableForTarget from the projection entry, not only as a unit call).\n6|(4) The source-race check named in this task: re-digest the source after the walk and classify a mutation DETECTED BEFORE PROJECTION — a changed byte, a changed size, an appended record and a replaced file each produce either a refusal or the unstable_archive form with source_not_quiescent, never a silently stable capture. Prove the ordering: the mutation check must run before any projection output is produced, and a mutant that moves it after projection must redden a test.\n7|(5) Workspace checkpoint and source head: build the closed WorkspaceBinding from the real repository state — logical_workspace_id, cwd_relative normalized beneath the Workspace Group root (escape attempts, absolute paths and .. segments refuse), sorted unique repository_remote_fingerprints[0..128], branch, head_digest, index_digest, working_tree_digest — and bind the source basis (ax_session with source Session/Record/Checkpoint/Provider Identity IDs, or external_native with a sanitized source reference). No member grants filesystem authority and no absolute source path becomes cross-host identity.\n8|(6) Blob discipline from 10.2 at the real seam: fsync the blob, verify its size and digest, then atomically install it in the object store (the landed internal/localstore ObjectStore through InstallRawBlob); descriptor chunks sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, starting at offset zero and covering exactly size bytes, index starting at zero and increasing by one, empty blob = size zero and no chunks; logs and errors record digest, size and media type only — ship a negative test that scans every emitted log/error for a byte sequence unique to a secret fixture payload.\n9|Tests: the full capture driven end to end over a fixture store through the production entry (positives and the whole refusal table), n-of-m ratios with call sites, crash/idempotency evidence at the blob-install and manifest-publish seams (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) proving a replayed capture installs the same blob and publishes no half-written manifest, a narrowing mutant per gate (drop the containment check, the pre/post equality, the class exclusion, the ordering of the race check, each bound) executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and a conformance matrix over every 13.14.1/10.2 clause you touch with an explicit stated bound for anything you do not execute. No `ax` CLI, no provider process and no network: the store is a fixture directory; state that bound.\n10|COMMON CONTRACT (non-first, non-final leaf of a Story whose predecessor leaves are already checkpointed). Normative authority: the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md headings named above; the v0.7.0 adoption (STORY-260917-110onn) may land on trunk during your run and is byte-identical in these sections — if it has landed when you refresh, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers. Reuse the landed owners (canonicaljson closed shapes, scalar, sessrepo/sessstate/sessquery, sessckpt, matjournal, crashgate, fencing, sessprofile, provhost/resumesmoke, hosttrust/peeridentity/sshtransport, rpcwire/hostchannel, sessadapter, terminalbackend, localstore, secprim/secconftest) and above all the packages your own predecessor leaf just added on this Story branch — never fork a second model of anything already modeled; extend or adopt, and say in the results which existing type or gate you extended. Traceability: do NOT edit internal/traceability (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf carries the registry bindings and the re-pin; document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix instead. Evidence contract (repository DoD): every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; negatives for every refusal; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__); crash/idempotency evidence for every durable write (landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern) or an explicit purity bound; conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; README package section with test commands and NO capability/CLI claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry newest-first. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q ALREADY EXISTS and its tip is your predecessor leaf's signed checkpoint commit — do not re-provision it, do not rebase it, do not commit on it, do not amend or revert the checkpoint, and never edit .task-board directly or self-accept. Your candidate is the UNCOMMITTED working tree on top of that checkpoint: exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Before you start, read the predecessor's landed delta (`git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree show --stat HEAD`) and its outcome resources so you extend it instead of restating it. If origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2g5be6` (LOGBOOK append conflicts are resolved with --replay-resolutions: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add {\"checkpoint_oid\": <the ORIGINAL checkpoint OID recorded before the refresh>, \"path\": \"LOGBOOK.md\", \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>} keeping every entry newest-first), then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that also appears in your `git status` and restore trunk content by hand — a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies of trunk-changed files into the candidate and they read as reverts (README/LOGBOOK stay purely additive; task-board.config.json must equal HEAD byte-for-byte). Before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite (30 commands as of trunk c3aae73 — STORY-260830-4qojoz added three bounded rpcwire fuzz gates; read the count from the candidate config rather than assuming it) once before handoff (command 5 is `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs — that is expected, do not shorten it; command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted … -check`). Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in — if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-2g5be6_results.md, TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2g5be6_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-2g5be6 --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.\n11|\n12|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n13|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n14|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n15|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n16|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n17|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n18|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n19|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.\n20|\n21|TRUNK STATE AT YOUR SPAWN (recorded 2026-09-18): origin/main is c3aae73 as of 2026-09-18T01:30Z and carries BOTH the v0.7.0 adoption (PR #52, commit 2fc6d50) and the mesh-RPC Story plus the resumesmoke deadline fix (PR #53 a12d1bd, PR #54 c3aae73) — internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md, internal/specpin/v0.7.0.lock.json, internal/catalog/catalog.v0.7.0.json with `catalog.Adopted = ReleaseV070`, and internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json. Your Story branch was cut before that. You are a MIDDLE leaf, so you do NOT touch internal/traceability at all (the final leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 carries the registry bindings and the pin) — but if origin/main moves before your handoff, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2g5be6` and then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old base> <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`: README.md and LOGBOOK.md moved on trunk with that landing, so keep your edits purely additive on top of the NEW content and never restore the old bytes. Once the refresh lands, cite SPEC.v0.7.0.md with the same heading numbers as the v0.6.0 sections named above.\n22|\n23|INHERITED ADVISORIES from the independent review that ACCEPTED the predecessor leaf (RUN-260918-3180f5 accepted TASK-260830-24z2b3 CR rev6 after closing an admit-hole where `encoding/json` rewrote invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and sealed it). It recorded three P3 measurement gaps \"for the sibling leaves\" — production is correct in each, but one member of a pinned class is unmeasured, which is precisely how this Story's earlier rounds went wrong twice. Read them in TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev6.md, close the ones your scope touches, and say in your results which you closed and which you deliberately left to the final leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2:\n24|- **P3-ε `hasUnknownClass` is pinned only for the INCLUDED unknown member.** The narrowing `if item.Class == \"unknown\" && item.Included()` (`capturebuild.go:418`, `R6-unknown-ignores-excluded`) **SURVIVED the whole package suite 2/2**. Under it, driven through the production entries (`logs/probe-under-mutant-unknown-excluded.log`): `BuildCaptureManifest` seals `raw_complete=true` for a manifest carrying an excluded unknown-class item (spec: \"Unknown makes raw completeness false\"), `DecodeCaptureManifest` admits `raw_complete=true` beside that item, and `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` no long\n25|- **P3-ζ the lone-surrogate member is unpinned at the shared text gate.** `R6-text-helper-lone-title` (`validText` admits exactly one WTF-8 lone-surrogate title) **SURVIVED 2/2**: the only committed lone-surrogate row (`capture_source_identity_native_lone_surrogate`) reaches `SanitizeNativeKey`'s own `utf8.ValidString`, never `validText`. §1.6 names lone surrogates explicitly and the rev4 fix scope named them; production refuses them at every site (section T, `lone` rows). Fix: one lone-surrogate row through a `validText` site (e.g. the title) plus a harness row.\n26|- **P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone admits identity fields decoding refuses.** Section T5: a 513-character native session ID or opaque identity, kind `bogus`, and a zero `LogicalWorkspaceID` (sealed as `\"\"`) are all encoded. Both production callers (`IdentityDigest`, `buildCaptureManifest`) re-decode and refuse (T5-2, T5-3), and the doc comment says \"renders one validated identity\", so no production path seals them; but the exported entry now advertises \"encoding never admits what decoding refused\" for extensions and native keys while still trusting the caller for bounds, vocabulary and","final_result":true}}}
