{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c593","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":292,"recorded_at":1780531400000579,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b27f-8f51-77a3-bef5-c0b8181c558b"},"task_id":"01a0b27f-8f51-77a3-bef5-c0b8181c558b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b27f-8f51-77a3-bef5-c0b8181c558b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 Results — implement-native-capture-and-source-race-check\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`) on the predecessor\n5|checkpoint `2f844bb` (Story branch over trunk `a12d1bd`); no commit\n6|on the Story branch. `origin/main` is `c3aae73` at handoff, unchanged\n7|since spawn, so no `refresh-candidate` ran.\n8|\n9|## Delivered\n10|\n11|`internal/clonesnap` implements the capture operation over a real\n12|on-disk provider store (second leaf of STORY-260830-1cyj0q):\n13|\n14|- Contained walk: every payload open descends from the verified\n15|  store-root handle through the landed `secprim` Guard. A symlinked\n16|  intermediate component, a trailing symlink, a FIFO, and a\n17|  directory each refuse before any payload byte is read, naming the\n18|  member. Enumeration observes names only; nothing enumerated is\n19|  opened except through the Guard, so capture never escapes the\n20|  store root.\n21|- Classification into the closed nine-class vocabulary: included\n22|  rows carry descriptor + count and no reason; excluded rows carry\n23|  null content and a stable reason. The four always-excluded\n24|  classes are never opened — a fixture store carries one member of\n25|  each and the suite proves its bytes reach no blob, manifest, log\n26|  line, or error string. `unknown` seals as captured and drives\n27|  `raw_complete=false`, blocking `maximal_safe` through the landed\n28|  gate at the projection entry.\n29|- Boundary from measured evidence: `stable` seals the closed proof\n30|  kind, generation, equal pre/post digests, and idle facts; an\n31|  equal-size differing-bytes fixture proves size equality never\n32|  admits stable. `unstable_archive` seals generation, pre/post\n33|  digests, `source_not_quiescent`, the explicit acknowledgement,\n34|  and `target_projection_forbidden=true`, is core-created for\n35|  archive-only output, and the projection entry refuses it for any\n36|  target branch via the landed G2 gate.\n37|- The named source-race check: the walk reads every included\n38|  member twice (capture + pre, then post) and enumerates twice; a\n39|  changed byte, changed size, appended record, replaced file, or\n40|  removed file refuses — or seals `unstable_archive` when archival\n41|  was explicitly acknowledged — never silently stable. The gate\n42|  precedes every seal and every projection output (ORDER-PIN in\n43|  `Capture` and `CaptureAndProject`); the two ordering mutants\n44|  move it after and both killers redden.\n45|- Workspace checkpoint and source head: the closed\n46|  `WorkspaceBinding` built from observed state (logical workspace,\n47|  normalized cwd beneath the group root, sorted unique\n48|  fingerprints, branch, head/index/tree digests) and sealed through\n49|  the landed decoder; escapes, absolute paths, dot segments, and\n50|  unobserved cwds refuse. The source basis binds `ax_session` IDs\n51|  or a sanitized `external_native` reference through the capture\n52|  manifest.\n53|- Blob discipline: descriptors seal through\n54|  `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` plus the landed agreement\n55|  check (sorted contiguous chunks from zero, empty blob without\n56|  chunks, multi-chunk layout pinned); payloads install via the\n57|  landed `InstallRawBlob`; manifests and receipts publish via\n58|  `PutBlob`. Past-128 GiB members fail with\n59|  `capability_unavailable` before any manifest is published\n60|  (sparse-file row pins the default without reading 128 GiB).\n61|- Crash/idempotency: a real-SIGKILL child killed between the raw\n62|  and capture publishes leaves one verified raw manifest and no\n63|  capture manifest; the identical replay converges with\n64|  byte-identical manifests, and a triple project verifies and\n65|  reuses every blob.\n66|\n67|Every artifact is produced through the landed `clonebundle`\n68|builders and re-decoded before publish or return; no second model\n69|exists. No `ax` CLI, provider process, or network; no\n70|`internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin).\n71|\n72|## AC coverage: 17 of 17 rows driven\n73|\n74|See `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`: every row names its\n75|production call site and driving test. Ratio: **17 of 17 AC rows\n76|driven**.\n77|\n78|## Validation reran (this run, final tree)\n79|\n80|- Commands 1-3 (gofmt check, build, vet): exit 0 (`cmd01.log`,\n81|  `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n82|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1`): exit 0, 39 packages ok,\n83|  zero FAIL (`cmd04.log`)\n84|- Command 5 (race gate): exit 0 in four bounded package groups\n85|  a/b/c/d (10+10+10+9 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE`, zero FAIL)\n86|  instead of one 25m call, per the headless time bound\n87|  (`cmd05a.log` … `cmd05d.log`)\n88|- Command 6 (cover gate): exit 0 in two bounded groups (20+19\n89|  packages ok, zero FAIL) (`cmd06a.log`, `cmd06b.log`;\n90|  `internal/clonesnap` 86.9% statements)\n91|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): exit 0 (`cmd07.log` …\n92|  `cmd20.log`)\n93|- Command 21 (`tracecheck`): exit 0, bindings=68, clauses 49/569 —\n94|  unchanged, `internal/traceability` untouched (`cmd21.log`)\n95|- Command 22 (`cataloggen -adopted -check`): exit 0, empty output\n96|  (`cmd22.log`)\n97|- Commands 23-24 (`GOOS=linux/windows` builds): exit 0\n98|  (`cmd23.log`, `cmd24.log`)\n99|- Command 25 (JSON validation): exit 0 (`cmd25.log`)\n100|- Command 26 (`task-board validate`): exit 0; the 184 reported\n101|  issues are pre-existing `[MISSING_ACTIVITY]` warnings on\n102|  unrelated tasks, none naming this task (`cmd26.log`)\n103|- Command 27 (`git diff --check`): exit 0 (`cmd27.log`)\n104|- Package suite: exit 0 (`pkg-test.log`), 86.9% statements\n105|  (`pkg-cover.log`); package race exit 0 (`pkg-race.log`)\n106|- Mutant harness: 29/29 ok (28 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control), full\n107|  battery run twice with per-plant raw logs carrying subprocess\n108|  exits (`mutants/run1/*.log`, `mutants/run2/*.log`,\n109|  `mutants-run2.log`), `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no\n110|  `__pycache__`, tree restored (`git status` shows only candidate\n111|  paths after both runs)\n112|\n113|## Mutant rows (28 narrowing + 1 control)\n114|\n115|Containment: `N-contain-trailing`, `N-contain-intermediate`,\n116|`N-fifo` (forged bytes for exactly one member). Plan gate:\n117|`N-unplanned`, `N-plan-prefix` (token-preserving: exact→prefix\n118|match, killer drives full `Capture`), `N-plan-order`,\n119|`N-plan-sanitize`, `N-plan-class`. Exclusion: one row per\n120|always-excluded class. Presence: `N-required`, `N-optional`. Race:\n121|`N-race-narrow`, `N-race-order-capture`, `N-race-order-project`.\n122|Archive/admission: `N-explicit`, `N-g2`, `N-maximal`, `N-fidelity`.\n123|Bounds: `N-oversize`, `N-descriptor-empty`, `N-descriptor-offset`,\n124|`N-workspace-cwd`, `N-workspace-fingerprints`. Leak/crash:\n125|`N-log-leak`, `N-hook-crash`. Control: `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED.\n126|\n127|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n128|\n129|- No `ax` CLI, provider process, or network (fixture store);\n130|  Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`.\n131|- The sealed stable proof carries the gate-verified pre digest\n132|  for both capture digests; the ordering mutants prove the gate\n133|  precedes the seal.\n134|- Excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor\n135|  (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored\n136|  before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot).\n137|- Optional absent candidates seal as excluded\n138|  (`plan_optional_absent`); `MaxSingleBytes` mirrors the 7.8\n139|  `ResourceLimits` per-object bound (default 137438953472).\n140|- The admission receipt proves admission and ordering only;\n141|  projection planning past admission is the final leaf's.\n142|- `internal/traceability` bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n143|\n144|## Attachments\n145|\n146|- `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`\n147|- `TASK-260830-2g5be6_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (27-command suite\n148|  logs, package suite, 2×28+1 mutant battery with per-plant logs,\n149|  file manifest)","final_result":true}}}
