{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c597","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":294,"recorded_at":1780531400000583,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b27f-8f82-7522-9d0b-5be6336333a7"},"task_id":"01a0b27f-8f82-7522-9d0b-5be6336333a7","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b27f-8f82-7522-9d0b-5be6336333a7","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/conformance.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 Conformance Matrix\n2|\n3|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 1.6, 7.8,\n4|10.2, 13.14.1 (§7.8, §10.2 and §13.14.1 verified byte-identical to\n5|v0.6.0). Package: `internal/clonesnap`. Normative spec text is\n6|quoted from the pinned file; the prose here maps, never restates.\n7|Every artifact below is produced through the landed `clonebundle`\n8|builders named in the call-site column; the\n9|`internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md` clause map carries the same\n10|rows with the landed-owner reuse table.\n11|\n12|## AC coverage: 17 of 17 rows driven\n13|\n14|Every row is driven through the named production entry point by the\n15|named committed test. Prose ratio: **17 of 17 AC rows driven**.\n16|\n17|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test |\n18||---|---|---|---|\n19|| 1 | Capture walk yields sorted unique raw entries from real bytes: sanitized key, class, byte count, blob ID, descriptor ID | `Capture` → `walkAndMeasure`, `BuildRawObjectManifest` | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureIsByteIdenticalAcrossRuns` |\n20|| 2 | Containment: symlinked intermediate, trailing symlink, FIFO, directory refuse before any payload open with the member named; capture never escapes the store root | `openMember` via `secprim.Guard`, `blockedAncestor`, `intermediatePrefix` | `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO/DirectoryMember/ParentPlanKey` |\n21|| 3 | Nine-class classification; included carries descriptor + count and no reason, excluded carries null content + stable reason; one item per plan candidate | `checkPlan` via `ValidCaptureClass`, `sealAndPublish` | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded`, `TestCaptureRefusesMysteryPlanClass/UnplannedMember/PrefixSibling/RequiredMissing/DuplicatePlanKey` |\n22|| 4 | credential/machine_auth/runtime_state/transient_lock always excluded; bytes never reach a blob, a manifest, a log line, or an error string | `excludedClass` (never opened) | `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` |\n23|| 5 | unknown drives raw_complete=false and blocks maximal_safe through the projection entry | `sealAndPublish`, `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete/MaximalSafeAdmitsComplete/StrictExactAdmitsUnknown` |\n24|| 6 | Stable boundary from real evidence: closed proof kind, generation, equal pre/post digests, idle facts | `sealAndPublish` via `buildBoundary` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureImmutableSnapshotProof`, `TestCaptureRefusesUnknownProofKind/IdleCouplingViolation/SnapshotIdentityCoupling/EmptyGeneration` |\n25|| 7 | Size equality is never proof: equal-size differing bytes refuse stable | `checkSourceRace` via `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte` |\n26|| 8 | unstable_archive carries generation, pre/post digests, source_not_quiescent, explicit ack, target_projection_forbidden; core-created, archive-only, never enters a target branch (projection entry) | `raceOutcome`, `sealAndPublish` (`Core: true`), `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable/ArchiveRequiresExplicit`, `TestProjectRefusesUnstable/RefusesUnstableDirect` |\n27|| 9 | Race check: changed byte, changed size, appended record, replaced file each refuse or seal unstable_archive, never silently stable | `walkAndMeasure`, `measurePost`, `gateSourceRace` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte/ChangedSize/AppendedRecord/ReplacedFile/RemovedFile`, `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` |\n28|| 10 | Mutation check runs before any seal or projection output | `Capture`, `CaptureAndProject` (ORDER-PIN) | `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest`, `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` |\n29|| 11 | WorkspaceBinding from real state: normalized cwd, sorted unique fingerprints[0..128], branch, head/index/tree digests | `CheckpointWorkspace` via `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceSealsObservedState/RelativeCwd/RootCwd/UnsortedFingerprints/DuplicateFingerprint/TooManyFingerprints/BadDigest/BadWorkspaceID`, `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes` |\n30|| 12 | No member grants filesystem authority: escapes, absolute paths, dot segments, unobserved cwds refuse | `workspaceCwdRelative` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesEscape/DotSegments/MissingCwd/FileCwd/SymlinkRoot` |\n31|| 13 | Source basis bound: ax_session IDs or sanitized external_native reference | `Capture` via `buildSourceBasis` (landed) | `TestCaptureExternalNativeBasis`, `TestCaptureRefusesMixedSourceBasis/UnknownBasisKind/UnsanitizedExternalRef` |\n32|| 14 | Blob install fsyncs, verifies, atomically installs; replayed capture installs the same blobs and publishes no half-written manifest | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` (real SIGKILL + replay convergence), `TestProjectIsIdempotent`, `TestCaptureHookFires` |\n33|| 15 | Descriptor chunks sorted, contiguous, non-overlapping, from zero, covering size; empty blob has no chunks; past-128 GiB fails with capability_unavailable before a partial manifest | `BuildBlobDescriptor` via `CalculateObjectIdentity` + `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestCaptureEmptyMemberSealsEmptyBlob/MultiChunkMember/DescriptorAgreementEndToEnd/RefusesOversizedMember/RefusesSparseOversizedMember`, `TestDefaultMaxSingleBytesIs128GiB` |\n34|| 16 | Logs and errors record digest, size, media type only | `CaptureLog` (no byte parameter) | `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (log + error scan) |\n35|| 17 | Fidelity profiles strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only; stable captures admit with a sealed receipt, unknown profiles refuse | `AdmitForTarget`, `BuildAdmissionReceipt` | `TestProjectAdmitsStableEveryProfile`, `TestProjectRefusesUnknownProfile` |\n36|\n37|## Negative/refusal evidence\n38|\n39|Every refusal above fails when the gate admits what it must reject:\n40|the 28 narrowing mutants in `internal/clonesnap/testdata/mutant_harness.py`\n41|weaken each gate to admit exactly one forbidden member and the named\n42|killer fails (28 KILLED, 1 harmless SURVIVED control). The\n43|token-preserving row `N-plan-prefix` keeps comparing against the\n44|planned keys while changing exact match to prefix match, and its\n45|killer drives the full `Capture` entry. Per-plant raw logs with\n46|subprocess exits are in the producer evidence tar (`mutants/run1/`).\n47|\n48|## Landed-owner reuse (not new behavior, cited not counted)\n49|\n50|| Scope | Owner | Evidence |\n51||---|---|---|\n52|| Capture contracts (manifests, items, basis, boundary, identities, generations) | `internal/clonebundle` (`Build*`, `Decode*`, `Refuse*`, `SanitizeNativeKey`, `CheckDigestsEqual`, `ValidCaptureClass`) | predecessor suite green in this run; every artifact here produced through those builders |\n53|| Section 7.8 operation frames | `internal/sessadapter` | landed suite green in this run; this package consumes plan keys/classes, not adapter frames |\n54|| Section 10.2 crash/idempotency discipline (fsync, atomic no-replace, quarantine) | `internal/localstore` | landed fault suites green in this run; delegation proven by the crash test + `TestProjectIsIdempotent` |\n55|| Containment walk (openat-relative, symlink/FIFO refusal) | `internal/secprim` (`Guard.Open`, `CheckMemberPath`, `OpenNoFollowDir`) | landed suites green in this run; every payload open here goes through `Guard.Open` |\n56|| Scalar gates + character string measure | `internal/environ`, `internal/scalar` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceMultibyteBranch`, owner batteries green in this run |\n57|\n58|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n59|\n60|- No `ax` CLI, no provider process, no network: the store is a\n61|  fixture directory. Section 7.8 operation wiring stays\n62|  `sessadapter`-owned.\n63|- The sealed stable proof carries the gate-verified pre digest for\n64|  both capture digests (production bytes identical to sealing the\n65|  measurement); the ordering mutants prove the gate precedes the\n66|  seal.\n67|- Excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor\n68|  (excluded bytes are never opened by design); presence, shape,\n69|  and size changes still race.\n70|- Sub-walk transient swaps restored before the post measurement\n71|  are below the floor (no filesystem snapshot); persistent changes\n72|  race and install-time verification still guards the read bytes.\n73|- Optional included-class candidates absent from the store seal as\n74|  excluded rows (`plan_optional_absent`); required ones refuse.\n75|- `MaxSingleBytes` mirrors the Section 7.8 `ResourceLimits`\n76|  per-object bound; zero selects 137438953472.\n77|- The admission receipt proves admission and ordering only;\n78|  projection planning past admission is the final leaf's.\n79|- `internal/traceability` bindings and re-pin (Story FINAL leaf).","final_result":true}}}
