{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c59b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":296,"recorded_at":1780531400000587,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b27f-8f2c-7483-b9d5-62b1b47fe29d"},"task_id":"01a0b27f-8f2c-7483-b9d5-62b1b47fe29d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b27f-8f2c-7483-b9d5-62b1b47fe29d","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 1\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-cee501 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2g5be6-1` revision 1, base\n5|`2f844bb49702a860c1199a6a2a0ca6a5cc878197` (the predecessor's checkpoint on the\n6|Story branch), candidate tree `31c0f23c3424e3fce3b23f736022cf91d1783122` (22\n7|paths; patch sha256 `d52c146e9c715d048d6cc86595166b8d065dc1baff6e83683d2a6b6a1745397f`,\n8|verified equal to `git diff 2f844bb 31c0f23`). The live Story worktree's\n9|temp-index tree OID equalled `31c0f23c…` before and after this review and\n10|`git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonesnap/`;\n11|the worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched.\n12|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines 10331–10546),\n13|§10.2 (4851–4900), §7.8 (3738–3925), re-extracted and diffed member-for-member\n14|against the candidate. (The reviewer brief's \"Section 4.C / terminalbackend\"\n15|paragraph is a copy from another leaf; this review covers the capture scope the\n16|task and producer brief define.)\n17|\n18|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n19|\n20|Production is correct on every probe I drove: I found no admit-hole, no\n21|spec-fidelity gap, no fork of a landed gate that changes behaviour, and no\n22|containment escape. What blocks acceptance is the evidence contract, in exactly\n23|the shape the producer brief warned about: five of the seventeen AC rows claim\n24|closure through named tests that do not reach the named member (a narrowing\n25|survives the whole committed suite 2/2 while the row's tests stay green), one\n26|of them a §10.2 MUST whose three cited tests never look at a payload blob; and\n27|the three inherited P3 advisories the brief required the producer to close or\n28|explicitly defer are neither closed nor mentioned — the in-scope one (P3-ε)\n29|opens the maximal-safe hole at this leaf's own projection entry under the\n30|predecessor's surviving mutant. The rework is small and precise (section\n31|\"Rework scope\").\n32|\n33|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n34|31c0f23c…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-2g5be6/review-rev1/{candidate,pristine,probe,\n35|probe2,mut}`, `.task-board` artifact dropped, `diff -r` clean against\n36|`pristine` before use and after every battery). Every probe and plant drove a\n37|production entry (`Capture`, `CaptureAndProject`, `AdmitForTarget`,\n38|`CheckpointWorkspace`, `BuildBlobDescriptor`); `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` for\n39|every harness, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in any copy. Raw evidence:\n40|`TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (`logs/`, one raw `go test`\n41|log per plant per run under `logs/mutants/run{1,2}/` and\n42|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/`, `reviewer_mutants_rev1.py`,\n43|`zz_rev1_probe_test.go.txt`, `probes-rev1.log` with 117 `PROBE` lines (plus `probe-c12-pristine.log`), the\n44|`probe-under-mutant-*.log` executions of each survivor).\n45|\n46|## 0. Inherited advisories (predecessor verdict rev6, RUN-260918-3180f5)\n47|\n48|The producer brief: \"Read them … close the ones your scope touches, and say in\n49|your results which you closed and which you deliberately left to the final\n50|leaf.\" `TASK-260830-2g5be6_results.md`, the conformance matrix, TRACEABILITY.md\n51|and the LOGBOOK entry contain no mention of P3-ε, P3-ζ or P3-η (grep for\n52|`P3`, `advisor`, `inherit`, `lone`, `surrogate`, `EncodeNativeIdentity`,\n53|`excluded unknown`: zero hits).\n54|\n55|| Item | In this leaf's scope? | Grade |\n56||---|---|---|\n57|| P3-ε `hasUnknownClass` pinned only for the INCLUDED unknown member | **Yes** — AC row 5 \"unknown drives raw_complete=false and blocks maximal_safe through the projection entry\"; an optional absent `unknown` plan member seals an EXCLUDED unknown item here (`plan_optional_absent`) | **Silently dropped, still open.** `R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded` (the predecessor's exact narrowing at `capturebuild.go:418`) **SURVIVED the whole clonesnap suite 2/2**. Executed under it (`logs/probe-under-mutant-epsilon.log`): `Capture` seals `raw_complete=true` beside an excluded unknown item and **`AdmitForTarget(…, \"maximal_safe\")` returns nil** — the hole opens at this leaf's projection entry — while `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeAdmitsComplete`, `TestProjectStrictExactAdmitsUnknown` all PASS. Pristine is correct (probe B2: excluded unknown → `raw_complete=false`, `excluded_classes=[credential unknown]`, maximal_safe refused \"blocked by an unknown-class item\", strict_exact admits). |\n58|| P3-ζ lone surrogate unpinned at `validText` | No (titles/sessions belong to the normalization leaf) | Silently dropped — must be stated as deferred. |\n59|| P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone admits what decoding refuses | Partially — this leaf is a caller of `IdentityDigest`/`BuildCaptureManifest`, which re-decode | Silently dropped. Production here is safe: probe F1 drove a 513-character native ID, kind `bogus`, a zero workspace ID, `native\\xff` and `/abs/native` through `Capture`; every one refused (`native identity digest seals no undecodable identity: …`). The `CaptureRequest.SourceIdentity` \"is the sanitized NativeIdentity\" doc line should state that the entry re-validates it (it does), and the results must say η's TRACEABILITY line is the final leaf's or clonebundle's. |\n60|\n61|## Findings\n62|\n63|No P1.\n64|\n65|### P2 — evidence contract (claimed evidence does not reach the claim)\n66|\n67|- **P2-α Inflated AC ratio: \"17 of 17 rows driven\" at the member level is\n68|  12 of 17.** Five rows name tests that stay green while a narrowing admits\n69|  the row's own member; each plant SURVIVED the whole committed suite in two\n70|  independent runs and its admitted behaviour was executed under the plant:\n71|  - **Row 14 (§10.2 MUST \"before publishing a record that references a blob …\n72|    atomically install it\")** — `R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b` (exactly\n73|    `store/blob-b` sealed into the raw manifest, its blob never installed)\n74|    SURVIVED 2/2. Under it (`logs/probe-under-mutant-payload-skip.log`) the\n75|    three tests the matrix cites for the row — `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`,\n76|    `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates`, `TestProjectIsIdempotent` — all\n77|    PASS while the store holds 3 blobs (blob-a + two manifests) and the\n78|    published raw manifest references a blob-b that is not there. None of the\n79|    cited tests inspects a payload blob; only the manifest `Installed` flags\n80|    and blob counts are asserted. This is the whole payload half of the MUST,\n81|    not one member of it.\n82|  - **Row 8 \"unstable_archive … never enters a target branch (projection\n83|    entry)\"** — `R1-archive-emits-receipt` (the archive branch of\n84|    `CaptureAndProject` writes the archive capture manifest into the TARGET\n85|    sink before the G2 refusal) SURVIVED 2/2. Under it `TestProjectRefusesUnstable`,\n86|    `TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect` and `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt`\n87|    PASS while `target_blobs=1` (`logs/probe-under-mutant-archive-emits.log`).\n88|    The G2 refusal is pinned at the error only; the target sink is inspected\n89|    only under `RaceRefuse`. Pristine: probe C11 `target_blobs=0`.\n90|  - **Row 2 containment \"symlinked intermediate … refuse\"** —\n91|    `R1-blockedAncestor-optional` (drop the `blockedAncestor` guard from the\n92|    optional-absent branch) SURVIVED 2/2: an OPTIONAL plan member whose\n93|    intermediate is a symlink to an outside directory seals as\n94|    `plan_optional_absent` and the capture succeeds (`err=<nil> result=true`,\n95|    `logs/probe-under-mutant-blockedAncestor.log`) while\n96|    `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO` and\n97|    `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded` PASS. Every committed\n98|    symlink/FIFO row is `Required: true`. Pristine refuses (probes A3, A4:\n99|    `member symlink escape: link-escape/file`, `target special file`).\n100|  - **Row 9 race \"replaced file\"** — `R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash`\n101|    (a member the post measurement cannot re-read falls back to the captured\n102|    hash) SURVIVED 2/2 with all seven `TestCaptureRace*` rows green. The\n103|    admitted member is concrete: a member that grows PAST `MaxSingleBytes`\n104|    between the walk and the post measurement, and a member whose permission\n105|    is lost, both **seal `stable`** under the plant (`logs/probe-c12-under-mutant-post-fallback.log`:\n106|    `err=<nil> stable=true` twice) while pristine refuses both\n107|    (`logs/probe-c12-pristine.log`). The committed \"replaced file\" row\n108|    replaces with a readable regular file; retype-to-symlink is caught by the\n109|    enumeration shape, so the unreadable-regular-file class has no row.\n110|  - **Row 5 unknown** — the excluded-unknown member (P3-ε above).\n111|- **P2-β Inherited advisories neither closed nor deferred** (section 0). The\n112|  in-scope one is part of P2-α; the other two must be named as deferred in the\n113|  results so the final leaf inherits them on the record, not by accident.\n114|\n115|### P3 — prose that outruns the tests; rows that measure the wrong thing\n116|\n117|- **P3-γ A false justification stated in four places** (doc comment on\n118|  `sealAndPublish`, TRACEABILITY.md \"Stated bounds\", LOGBOOK \"ORDERING\",\n119|  results \"Bounds\"): \"sealing the raw post measurement instead would fail\n120|  closed under a reorder and leave the ordering unpinned\". Executed\n121|  (`logs/claim-post-sealed-under-reorder.log`): with `PostCaptureDigest:\n122|  state.post.String()` AND the producer's own `N-race-order-capture` reorder\n123|  applied together, `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest` still FAILS (\"mutated\n124|  capture sealed a raw manifest before the race gate\") — the raw manifest is\n125|  published before the boundary is built, so the ordering stays pinned either\n126|  way. The equivalence control `R1-stable-seals-post-as-pre` SURVIVED 2/2 as\n127|  it must (under the gate pre == post; probe C9 sealed post == measured post).\n128|  Sealing the pre value for `post_capture_digest` is not a defect, but the\n129|  reason given for it is false; seal the measured post digest (the member the\n130|  spec names) or reword the bound to what is true.\n131|- **P3-δ `N-workspace-cwd` measures the message, not admission.** Under the\n132|  row `/outside-workspace` is still refused by `scalar.ParseRelativePath`\n133|  (\"must not contain empty, dot, or parent segments\"); the killer reddens on\n134|  the missing literal \"escapes the workspace root\"\n135|  (`logs/mutants-producer/run1/N-workspace-cwd.log`). The line-120 escape check\n136|  is subsumed by the landed relative-path grammar on POSIX; state it as defence\n137|  in depth or make the row assert admission.\n138|- **P3-ε′ `N-exclude-*` rows are killed by the landed builder, not by the leak\n139|  scan** (`raw object entry[0] class \"credential\" is outside the raw subset`);\n140|  under those plants the excluded bytes WERE opened and installed before the\n141|  seal refused. The scan is load-bearing — my `R1-excluded-bytes-into-blob`\n142|  (orphan blob, no manifest entry, no log line) is KILLED 2/2 by\n143|  `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` — but the harness should carry that row so the\n144|  claim \"bytes never reach a blob\" is measured by the scan, not inferred from a\n145|  builder refusal.\n146|- **P3-ζ′ Second spelling of the four-profile fidelity vocabulary.**\n147|  `internal/sessadapter/operations.go:535` already holds the §7.8\n148|  `fidelityProfiles` table (unexported); `clonesnap.validFidelityProfile` is a\n149|  second copy. Not a behavioural fork, but the final leaf will need the same\n150|  vocabulary — export one owner.\n151|\n152|### Informational (no action required unless cheap)\n153|\n154|- `CheckpointWorkspace` admits a relative `WorkspaceRoot` (probe E5,\n155|  resolves against the process cwd; `secprim.NewGuard` requires absolute for\n156|  the store root) and records `cwd_relative=\"link\"` for a symlink inside the\n157|  root that points outside (probe E1) — lexically contained, no authority\n158|  granted; worth a stated line.\n159|- Seal-time refusals (identity, basis, proof coupling, generation) run after\n160|  the walk, so payload blobs are already installed as content-addressed\n161|  orphans when they refuse (probe F1: `blobs=2`). No manifest is published;\n162|  fail-fast validation of request scalars before the walk would be cheaper.\n163|- `NativeSessionID` and `SourceIdentity.NativeSessionID` may disagree (probe\n164|  F6) — spec-silent.\n165|- The admission receipt `urn:ax:internal:clonesnap-admission-receipt` is a\n166|  package-internal artifact carried only to pin ordering; it is documented as\n167|  such. The final leaf should replace it with the real projection output or\n168|  keep the bound explicit.\n169|- Enumeration walks path strings (`os.ReadDir`/`os.Lstat`) while every open is\n170|  openat-relative through the Guard; TRACEABILITY states this bound. A\n171|  directory→symlink swap between `Lstat` and `ReadDir` could list outside\n172|  NAMES into an unplanned-member refusal; no byte can follow (Guard root\n173|  binding refuses, probe A8/A1).\n174|\n175|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n176|\n177|1. **Spec fidelity** (`logs/probes-rev1.log`, 117 probe lines): Raw Object\n178|   Manifest entries from real bytes, sorted, sanitized, blob/descriptor IDs\n179|   recomputed (A9: 11 plan-key shapes refuse — `./`, `//`, trailing `/`, `.`,\n180|   `..`, `store/..`, backslash, NUL, `\\n`, `%2e%2e`); `excluded_classes`\n181|   exactly the excluded-row classes including a `plan_optional_absent`\n182|   durable class (B1); one item per plan candidate; always-excluded classes\n183|   never opened — 3 blobs total for a five-member store (B4), an excluded\n184|   member that is a symlink to an outside secret is never followed (A6);\n185|   every stable-proof kind with its coupling rule, 13 combinations (F2);\n186|   generation and external-ref bounds 512/513 in characters (F3: 512\n187|   two-byte characters admit; F4); timestamp/UUIDv7 stamps refuse (F5); the\n188|   §10.2 example reproduces byte-exactly — `ax-example\\n` seals\n189|   `descriptor_id sha256:390c8f21…` and `blob_id sha256:9c21bad6…` (D3);\n190|   chunking at 4194303/4194304/4194305/8388608/8388609 → 1/1/2/2/3 chunks\n191|   (D2); per-object bound at 19/18 bytes both directions (D4); manifests\n192|   addressed by the SHA-256 of their sealed bytes (D5).\n193|2. **Containment** at depth 3 with the symlink in the MIDDLE component\n194|   (A1: `member symlink escape: a/link/file`, no outside byte in the store),\n195|   FIFO at depth 2 named as `target special file` never \"open failed\" and\n196|   never stalling (A2), optional FIFO (A3), inside-store symlink (A5),\n197|   unplanned symlink (A7), symlinked store root (A8), dangling intermediate\n198|   and trailing symlinks (A10/A11). Producer rows `N-contain-*`, `N-fifo`\n199|   KILLED 2/2.\n200|3. **Exclusion**: four secret sequences reach no blob, manifest, log line or\n201|   error string on pristine; `R1-excluded-bytes-into-blob` KILLED 2/2 proves\n202|   the blob scan is load-bearing; refusal strings on the containment path\n203|   carry no outside bytes (B6).\n204|4. **Source race**: true `O_APPEND` append (C1), equal-size symlink swap\n205|   (C2), excluded member size change (C3), new directory (C5) all refuse\n206|   naming the member; equal-size content change of an EXCLUDED member and an\n207|   mtime-only touch seal stable (C4/C6 — the stated bound, confirmed);\n208|   archive policy seals `unstable_archive` with the two MEASURED digests and\n209|   the raw manifest carrying the pre-mutation bytes (C7); archive policy on a\n210|   quiet store seals stable (C8); a race through `CaptureAndProject` leaves\n211|   both sinks without manifests or receipts (C10); the archive form through\n212|   the projection entry publishes to the capture store, target sink empty,\n213|   G2 refusal (C11). `R1-size-equality-is-proof` (size-only comparison)\n214|   KILLED 2/2 by seven tests; `R1-archive-seals-stable`, `R1-unstable-not-core`\n215|   KILLED 2/2; `R1-hook-after-post-measure` (seam control) KILLED 2/2.\n216|5. **Ordering**: producer rows `N-race-order-capture` / `N-race-order-project`\n217|   KILLED 2/2; the reorder is killed with either digest sealed (P3-γ).\n218|6. **Crash/idempotency**: the producer's real-SIGKILL child reproduced 2/2\n219|   (`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` in both harness runs and the\n220|   suite); my own SIGKILL at `AfterWalk` (`TestRev1ProbeCrashAfterWalk`,\n221|   H1): 2 payload blobs, 0 manifests, 0 staged temp files left; the replay\n222|   publishes both manifests (`raw_installed=true capture_installed=true`),\n223|   changes no payload blob, and is byte-identical to a clean capture.\n224|   `R1-publish-under-manifest-id` KILLED 2/2 (the store verifies the digest of\n225|   what it installs).\n226|7. **Blob discipline** on pristine: both payload blobs installed under their\n227|   content digests (D1); `R1-descriptor-media-uppercase` KILLED 2/2 (landed\n228|   closed-shape validator in the path); `R1-oversize-boundary-off-by-one`\n229|   KILLED 2/2.\n230|8. **Admission**: raw-as-capture, trailing data, empty, truncated refuse at\n231|   the decoder through `AdmitForTarget` (G1); a forged `raw_complete:true`\n232|   beside an unknown item refuses (G2); the receipt carries identities only\n233|   (G3); nil target sink refuses before any capture (G4). `N-g2`, `N-maximal`,\n234|   `N-fidelity` KILLED 2/2.\n235|9. **Workspace**: 128 fingerprints admit, 129 refuse; branch `\"\"` refuses, 1\n236|   char admits, 1024/1025 characters pinned by the producer; `sha1:` and\n237|   uppercase digests refuse (E3/E4); `./work`, `work/`, `work//trees`,\n238|   `work/trees/alpha/.`, `..`, NUL and `/` refuse, `.` admits (E2); a bad\n239|   workspace refuses before any install (E6).\n240|10. **Producer harness reproduced**: 28 KILLED + `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED,\n241|    twice, in the isolated copy; tree `diff -r` clean after each run; 29 raw\n242|    per-plant logs with `# exit=` per run.\n243|11. **Hygiene**: `gofmt -l` empty; `go vet` clean; `go build ./...`;\n244|    `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows` builds exit 0; `tracecheck` exit 0\n245|    (bindings=68, clauses 49/569 — `internal/traceability` untouched);\n246|    `cataloggen -adopted … -check` exit 0; `git diff --check` clean; package\n247|    `-race` ok (0 DATA RACE), cover 86.9%; neighbour suites (clonebundle,\n248|    localstore, secprim, canonicaljson, scalar, environ) ok. Changed paths are\n249|    exactly the 22 candidate paths; README additive with no capability/CLI\n250|    claim; LOGBOOK entry newest-first; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`. The CR\n251|    validation log reports `required=30 green=30` (the candidate config\n252|    carries 27 commands; the control root 30); the producer evidence archive\n253|    is a real gzip with 93 `MANIFEST.sha256` rows all OK, zero foreign\n254|    artifacts, cmd04 39 packages ok, race groups 0 DATA RACE\n255|    (`sessquery 379.6s`). I did not rerun the 25-minute whole-repository race\n256|    gate; I accept it from the CR validation log and ran `-race` on the\n257|    package.\n258|\n259|## Reviewer mutation battery (`reviewer_mutants_rev1.py`, whole committed suite as killer, 2 runs, identical verdicts)\n260|\n261|| Row | Kind | Verdict | Killers |\n262||---|---|---|---|\n263|| R1-blockedAncestor-optional | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 2) |\n264|| R1-excluded-bytes-into-blob | add-write | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureExcludesSecrets |\n265|| R1-size-equality-is-proof | widening | KILLED 2/2 | 7 tests |\n266|| R1-archive-seals-stable | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | 3 tests |\n267|| R1-archive-emits-receipt | add-write | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 8) |\n268|| R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 14) |\n269|| R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 9) |\n270|| R1-hook-after-post-measure | seam control | KILLED 2/2 | 11 tests |\n271|| R1-descriptor-media-uppercase | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | 40 tests |\n272|| R1-unstable-not-core | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | 3 tests |\n273|| R1-publish-under-manifest-id | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | 29 tests |\n274|| R1-oversize-boundary-off-by-one | narrowing | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember |\n275|| R1-stable-seals-post-as-pre | equivalence control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n276|| R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded | narrowing (inherited ε) | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P2-α row 5) |\n277|| C-rev1-comment | harmless control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n278|\n279|Measured ratio: 17 of 17 AC rows reached by a named test through a production\n280|entry; **12 of 17 closed at the member level** (rows 2, 5, 8, 9, 14 each carry\n281|a surviving narrowing whose admitted behaviour was executed above).\n282|\n283|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n284|\n285|1. Row 14: a committed test that asserts every raw-manifest entry's blob is\n286|   present in the store after `Capture` (and after the crash replay), plus a\n287|   harness row of the `R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b` shape.\n288|2. Row 8: assert the TARGET sink is empty on the archive path of\n289|   `CaptureAndProject` (`TestProjectRefusesUnstable`), plus a harness row of\n290|   the `R1-archive-emits-receipt` shape.\n291|3. Row 2: one `Required: false` member behind a symlinked intermediate (and\n292|   one optional FIFO) through `Capture`, plus a harness row narrowing the\n293|   optional-absent branch.\n294|4. Row 9: one race row where a member becomes unreadable at post time without\n295|   changing shape (grown past `MaxSingleBytes`, or `chmod 000`), plus a\n296|   harness row of the `R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash` shape.\n297|5. Row 5 / P3-ε: one optional absent `unknown` plan member driving\n298|   `raw_complete=false` and `AdmitForTarget(maximal_safe)` refusal, plus a\n299|   harness row of the `R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded` shape (the\n300|   plant lives in clonebundle; the killer lives here — say so).\n301|6. Results: a section naming P3-ε closed and P3-ζ / P3-η deferred to the final\n302|   leaf (or closed), and the measured ratio.\n303|7. P3-γ: seal `state.post` for `post_capture_digest` or reword the bound in\n304|   the four places; P3-δ: reword the `N-workspace-cwd` note (defence in\n305|   depth, message-keyed) or assert admission; P3-ε′: add the orphan-blob leak\n306|   row to the shipped harness; P3-ζ′: note the duplicated fidelity vocabulary\n307|   as a bound for the final leaf (or export one owner).\n308|\n309|Checklist state left by this review: the four reviewer rows (Implementation\n310|matches AC; Solution fits project architecture; Tests green; Gate … attacked,\n311|not read) are unchecked; \"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence\n312|added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\" is checked. Status\n313|routed to `to-dev`.","final_result":true}}}
