{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c59f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":298,"recorded_at":1780531400000591,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"call_id":"call_01a0b27f88cc77b98951a09d37c45ede","text":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 1\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-cee501 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2g5be6-1` revision 1, base\n5|`2f844bb49702a860c1199a6a2a0ca6a5cc878197` (the predecessor's checkpoint on the\n6|Story branch), candidate tree `31c0f23c3424e3fce3b23f736022cf91d1783122` (22\n7|paths; patch sha256 `d52c146e9c715d048d6cc86595166b8d065dc1baff6e83683d2a6b6a1745397f`,\n8|verified equal to `git diff 2f844bb 31c0f23`). The live Story worktree's\n9|temp-index tree OID equalled `31c0f23c…` before and after this review and\n10|`git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonesnap/`;\n11|the worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched.\n12|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines 10331–10546),\n13|§10.2 (4851–4900), §7.8 (3738–3925), re-extracted and diffed member-for-member\n14|against the candidate. (The reviewer brief's \"Section 4.C / terminalbackend\"\n15|paragraph is a copy from another leaf; this review covers the capture scope the\n16|task and producer brief define.)\n17|\n18|## Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED → `to-dev`\n19|\n20|Production is correct on every probe I drove: I found no admit-hole, no\n21|spec-fidelity gap, no fork of a landed gate that changes behaviour, and no\n22|containment escape. What blocks acceptance is the evidence contract, in exactly\n23|the shape the producer brief warned about: five of the seventeen AC rows claim\n24|closure through named tests that do not reach the named member (a narrowing\n25|survives the whole committed suite 2/2 while the row's tests stay green), one\n26|of them a §10.2 MUST whose three cited tests never look at a payload blob; and\n27|the three inherited P3 advisories the brief required the producer to close or\n28|explicitly defer are neither closed nor mentioned — the in-scope one (P3-ε)\n29|opens the maximal-safe hole at this leaf's own projection entry under the\n30|predecessor's surviving mutant. The rework is small and precise (section\n31|\"Rework scope\").\n32|\n33|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n34|31c0f23c…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-2g5be6/review-rev1/{candidate,pristine,probe,\n35|probe2,mut}`, `.task-board` artifact dropped, `diff -r` clean against\n36|`pristine` before use and after every battery). Every probe and plant drove a\n37|production entry (`Capture`, `CaptureAndProject`, `AdmitForTarget`,\n38|`CheckpointWorkspace`, `BuildBlobDescriptor`); `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` for\n39|every harness, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in any copy. Raw evidence:\n40|`TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (`logs/`, one raw `go test`\n41|log per plant per run under `logs/mutants/run{1,2}/` and\n42|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/`, `reviewer_mutants_rev1.py`,\n43|`zz_rev1_probe_test.go.txt`, `probes-rev1.log` with 117 `PROBE` lines (plus `probe-c12-pristine.log`), the\n44|`probe-under-mutant-*.log` executions of each survivor).\n45|\n46|## 0. Inherited advisories (predecessor verdict rev6, RUN-260918-3180f5)\n47|\n48|The producer brief: \"Read them … close the ones your scope touches, and say in\n49|your results which you closed and which you deliberately left to the final\n50|leaf.\" `TASK-260830-2g5be6_results.md`, the conformance matrix, TRACEABILITY.md\n51|and the LOGBOOK entry contain no mention of P3-ε, P3-ζ or P3-η (grep for\n52|`P3`, `advisor`, `inherit`, `lone`, `surrogate`, `EncodeNativeIdentity`,\n53|`excluded unknown`: zero hits).\n54|\n55|| Item | In this leaf's scope? | Grade |\n56||---|---|---|\n57|| P3-ε `hasUnknownClass` pinned only for the INCLUDED unknown member | **Yes** — AC row 5 \"unknown drives raw_complete=false and blocks maximal_safe through the projection entry\"; an optional absent `unknown` plan member seals an EXCLUDED unknown item here (`plan_optional_absent`) | **Silently dropped, still open.** `R1-clonebundle-unknown-ignores-excluded` (the predecessor's exact narrowing at `capturebuild.go:418`) **SURVIVED the whole clonesnap suite 2/2**. Executed under it (`logs/probe-under-mutant-epsilon.log`): `Capture` seals `raw_complete=true` beside an excluded unknown item and **`AdmitForTarget(…, \"maximal_safe\")` returns nil** — the hole opens at this leaf's projection entry — while `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeAdmitsComplete`, `TestProjectStrictExactAdmitsUnknown` all PASS. Pristine is correct (probe B2: excluded unknown → `raw_complete=false`, `excluded_classes=[credential unknown]`, maximal_safe refused \"blocked by an unknown-class item\", strict_exact admits). |\n58|| P3-ζ lone surrogate unpinned at `validText` | No (titles/sessions belong to the normalization leaf) | Silently dropped — must be stated as deferred. |\n59|| P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone admits what decoding refuses | Partially — this leaf is a caller of `IdentityDigest`/`BuildCaptureManifest`, which re-decode | Silently dropped. Production here is safe: probe F1 drove a 513-character native ID, kind `bogus`, a zero workspace ID, `native\\xff` and `/abs/native` through `Capture`; every one refused (`native identity digest seals no undecodable identity: …`). The `CaptureRequest.SourceIdentity` \"is the sanitized NativeIdentity\" doc line should state that the entry re-validates it (it does), and the results must say η's TRACEABILITY line is the final leaf's or clonebundle's. |\n60|\n61|## Findings\n62|\n63|No P1.\n64|\n65|### P2 — evidence contract (claimed evidence does not reach the claim)\n66|\n67|- **P2-α Inflated AC ratio: \"17 of 17 rows driven\" at the member level is\n68|  12 of 17.** Five rows name tests that stay green while a narrowing admits\n69|  the row's own member; each plant SURVIVED the whole committed suite in two\n70|  independent runs and its admitted behaviour was executed under the plant:\n71|  - **Row 14 (§10.2 MUST \"before publishing a record that references a blob …\n72|    atomically install it\")** — `R1-skip-payload-install-blob-b` (exactly\n73|    `store/blob-b` sealed into the raw manifest, its blob never installed)\n74|    SURVIVED 2/2. Under it (`logs/probe-under-mutant-payload-skip.log`) the\n75|    three tests the matrix cites for the row — `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`,\n76|    `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates`, `TestProjectIsIdempotent` — all\n77|    PASS while the store holds 3 blobs (blob-a + two manifests) and the\n78|    published raw manifest references a blob-b that is not there. None of the\n79|    cited tests inspects a payload blob; only the manifest `Installed` flags\n80|    and blob counts are asserted. This is the whole payload half of the MUST,\n81|    not one member of it.\n82|  - **Row 8 \"unstable_archive … never enters a target branch (projection\n83|    entry)\"** — `R1-archive-emits-receipt` (the archive branch of\n84|    `CaptureAndProject` writes the archive capture manifest into the TARGET\n85|    sink before the G2 refusal) SURVIVED 2/2. Under it `TestProjectRefusesUnstable`,\n86|    `TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect` and `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt`\n87|    PASS while `target_blobs=1` (`logs/probe-under-mutant-archive-emits.log`).\n88|    The G2 refusal is pinned at the error only; the target sink is inspected\n89|    only under `RaceRefuse`. Pristine: probe C11 `target_blobs=0`.\n90|  - **Row 2 containment \"symlinked intermediate … refuse\"** —\n91|    `R1-blockedAncestor-optional` (drop the `blockedAncestor` guard from the\n92|    optional-absent branch) SURVIVED 2/2: an OPTIONAL plan member whose\n93|    intermediate is a symlink to an outside directory seals as\n94|    `plan_optional_absent` and the capture succeeds (`err=<nil> result=true`,\n95|    `logs/probe-under-mutant-blockedAncestor.log`) while\n96|    `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO` and\n97|    `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded` PASS. Every committed\n98|    symlink/FIFO row is `Required: true`. Pristine refuses (probes A3, A4:\n99|    `member symlink escape: link-escape/file`, `target special file`).\n100|  - **Row 9 race \"replaced file\"** — `R1-post-falls-back-to-captured-hash`\n101|    (a member the post measurement cannot re-read falls back to the captured\n102|    hash) SURVIVED 2/2 with all seven `TestCaptureRace*` rows green. The\n103|    admitted member is concrete: a member that grows PAST `MaxSingleBytes`\n104|    between the walk and the post measurement, and a member whose permission\n105|    is lost, both **seal `stable`** under the plant (`logs/probe-c12-under-mutant-post-fallback.log`:\n106|    `err=<nil> stable=true` twice) while pristine refuses both\n107|    (`logs/probe-c12-pristine.log`). The committed \"replaced file\" row\n108|    replaces with a readable regular file; retype-to-symlink is caught by the\n109|    enumeration shape, so the unreadable-regular-file class has no row.\n110|  - **Row 5 unknown** — the excluded-unknown member (P3-ε above).\n111|- **P2-β Inherited advisories neither closed nor deferred** (section 0). The\n112|  in-scope one is part of P2-α; the other two must be named as deferred in the\n113|  results so the final leaf inherits them on the record, not by accident.\n114|\n115|### P3 — prose that outruns the tests; rows that measure the wrong thing\n116|\n117|- **P3-γ A false justification