|  `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` — but the harness should carry that row so the\n144|  claim \"bytes never reach a blob\" is measured by the scan, not inferred from a\n145|  builder refusal.\n146|- **P3-ζ′ Second spelling of the four-profile fidelity vocabulary.**\n147|  `internal/sessadapter/operations.go:535` already holds the §7.8\n148|  `fidelityProfiles` table (unexported); `clonesnap.validFidelityProfile` is a\n149|  second copy. Not a behavioural fork, but the final leaf will need the same\n150|  vocabulary — export one owner.\n151|\n152|### Informational (no action required unless cheap)\n153|\n154|- `CheckpointWorkspace` admits a relative `WorkspaceRoot` (probe E5,\n155|  resolves against the process cwd; `secprim.NewGuard` requires absolute for\n156|  the store root) and records `cwd_relative=\"link\"` for a symlink inside the\n157|  root that points outside (probe E1) — lexically contained, no authority\n158|  granted; worth a stated line.\n159|- Seal-time refusals (identity, basis, proof coupling, generation) run after\n160|  the walk, so payload blobs are already installed as content-addressed\n161|  orphans when they refuse (probe F1: `blobs=2`). No manifest is published;\n162|  fail-fast validation of request scalars before the walk would be cheaper.\n163|- `NativeSessionID` and `SourceIdentity.NativeSessionID` may disagree (probe\n164|  F6) — spec-silent.\n165|- The admission receipt `urn:ax:internal:clonesnap-admission-receipt` is a\n166|  package-internal artifact carried only to pin ordering; it is documented as\n167|  such. The final leaf should replace it with the real projection output or\n168|  keep the bound explicit.\n169|- Enumeration walks path strings (`os.ReadDir`/`os.Lstat`) while every open is\n170|  openat-relative through the Guard; TRACEABILITY states this bound. A\n171|  directory→symlink swap between `Lstat` and `ReadDir` could list outside\n172|  NAMES into an unplanned-member refusal; no byte can follow (Guard root\n173|  binding