{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":425,"recorded_at":1780531400000845,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b27f-d150-70b3-999f-14897bcb914a"},"task_id":"01a0b27f-d150-70b3-999f-14897bcb914a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b27f-d150-70b3-999f-14897bcb914a","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/pred-verdict.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 6\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-3180f5 (claude-opus-5, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-24z2b3-6` revision 6, base\n5|`a12d1bd5102014790e4c1a36ccc2fcb2422e8f25` (current origin/main, carries the\n6|BUG-260918-354b03 resumesmoke fix), candidate tree\n7|`7a3784136c4f24bea753ea1bd860ccde35fddd87` (24 paths; patch sha256\n8|`40a273688d125702f7f580ff75d13a0711d7be1e3a9296ebae82a8408abf0319`, verified\n9|against the attached patch and against `git diff a12d1bd 7a37841`).\n10|Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines 10331–10546), §7.8\n11|(3738–3860), §10.2 (4851–4900) and the common logical data model §1.6\n12|(244–337); the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0 as the producer\n13|states. Revision 5 was never reviewed (its construction failed on the trunk\n14|time bomb); this review covers the whole revision 6, with the rev4 rework\n15|graded first.\n16|\n17|## Verdict: ACCEPTED → `accept_cr(TASK-260830-24z2b3, revision=6)`\n18|\n19|The P2-δ admit-hole that blocked revision 4 is closed at every Build-side\n20|string admission, not only at the two witnessed entries, and the four P3 items\n21|are fixed. My own attack of the whole revision found no admit-hole, no\n22|spec-fidelity gap, and no unreproduced claim: every probe I drove through a\n23|production entry refused what the pinned text forbids, and the sealed bytes\n24|never carried a substituted U+FFFD. What remains is three P3 measurement gaps\n25|(production correct, one member of a pinned class unmeasured) and a handful of\n26|informational notes, recorded below for the sibling leaves; none of them is a\n27|production defect or a reason to hold the leaf.\n28|\n29|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n30|7a37841…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-24z2b3/review-rev6/{candidate,pristine,probe}`,\n31|`.task-board` artifact dropped; the live worktree's temp-index tree OID was\n32|confirmed equal to `7a37841…` before anything ran and `git status` was\n33|` M LOGBOOK.md`, ` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonebundle/` before and after).\n34|The live Story worktree, index, branch and HEAD were never touched. Every probe\n35|and plant ran through the production entry points; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`\n36|for every harness, no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` written; the candidate copy diffed\n37|clean against the pristine copy after every battery. Raw evidence is in\n38|`TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-evidence-rev6.tar.gz` (`logs/`, `logs/mutants/`\n39|one raw `go test` log per plant per run with `# exit=`,\n40|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/` the shipped harness's per-plant logs,\n41|`reviewer_mutants_rev6.py`, `zz_rev6_probe*_test.go.txt`, the rev3/rev4 probe\n42|files re-executed on this tree).\n43|\n44|## 0. Rework verification — every rev4 finding graded\n45|\n46|| rev4 finding | Grade | Executed evidence (this run, new tree) |\n47||---|---|---|\n48|| P2-δ Build entries rewrite invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD and seal it; `BuildCaptureManifest`/`IdentityDigest` launder a native key past the sanitizer; `native\\xff` vs `native\\xfe` seal byte-identical | **fixed** | rev4 section K re-executed (`logs/probes-rev4-k-on-rev6.log`): K1–K13 all REFUSED `native key is not valid UTF-8`, K4 both sides refuse, K14 `IdentityDigest(op\\xff) == IdentityDigest(op\\ufffd)` is now false. rev4 section C re-executed (`logs/probes-rev4-on-rev6.log`): C1–C14, C16, C17 REFUSED (C15 — NUL/BEL in a title — is admitted; §1.6 permits control characters in text, only native keys refuse them). My own class attack (`logs/probes-rev6-text.log`, section T): **43 Build-side string admissions × 2 shapes (`\\xff` and the WTF-8 lone surrogate `\\xed\\xa0\\x80`) = 86 probes, 86 REFUSED, `sealed_has_FFFD=false` on every one** — session title, actor name/model/source_native_id, session source_native_session_id, session extension value/key; evidence native_type, reason code [0] and [1], native_session_id, native_event_id, event extension nested slice→map; capture identity native/opaque/kind, item exclusion_reason/key/extension, identity extension, manifest extension, stable and unstable boundary generation, external_source_ref; raw source_native_session_id, entry key, raw extension value/key/array/pointer/interface/struct-field/map[string]string/map[string]int-key/json.RawMessage; `IdentityDigest` native/opaque/kind; `EncodeNativeIdentity` native/opaque/kind/extension; `ParseGeneration`. Section T2: raw-byte Build inputs are refused at the environ frame gate — payload with raw `\\xff`, `\\ud800`, `\\udc00`, the `\"\\\\ud800\\udc00\"` decoy, WTF-8 bytes, a non-message payload, evidence tuple, workspace (branch and extensions), capture tuple, descriptor media_type; `json.RawMessage` and custom-`MarshalJSON` extension values emitting `\\xff` or `\\ud800` are refused too (T2-14/15/16), so the stated \"custom Marshaler trusted\" bound is stricter in practice than stated. Section T3: a legitimate U+FFFD in a title is admitted and sealed (the input carried it), overlong `\\xc0\\x80` and a code point beyond U+10FFFF refuse, `\\xff`/`\\xfe` titles both refuse (T3-6). Section T4: Decode refuses raw `\\xff`, `\\ud800` and the decoy at the frame. Mutation: **13 one-step-away narrowings KILLED 2/2** — per-site exemption of exactly the killer value at title, actor name, actor model, native_type, reason code, exclusion_reason, generation and identity kind (`R6-text-site-*`), walker arms (`R6-text-walk-skip-keys`, `-skip-struct`, `-skip-first-element`) and the encode-time sanitize for both native keys (`R6-encode-skip-opaque-sanitize`, `R6-encode-skip-native-sanitize` — the original hole, one member); producer `N-text-utf8` KILLED 2/2. |\n49|| P3-a″ evidence archive contaminated | **fixed** | `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (real gzip): 168 files, all matching the expected pattern (27 `cmd*.log`, `pkg-*.log`, 2×67 per-plant logs, two battery logs, `p3b-probe.log`, `MANIFEST.sha256`); `shasum -c MANIFEST.sha256` all OK (167 rows); zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc`; no foreign artifacts. |\n50|| P3-b″ TRACEABILITY over-claims the `-0`/`+`/leading-zero bound | **fixed** | Sentence now states `-0` admits (sealed as `0`), `+1`/`01` refuse at the frame; rev4 probes B3/B8 re-executed on this tree agree (`logs/probes-rev4-on-rev6.log`). |\n51|| P3-c″ build-side reason-code duplicate unmeasured | **fixed** | `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/evidence/reasons_duplicate` exists; `N-reason-codes-dup-build` KILLED 2/2 in the shipped harness; my R10q (duplicate raw_refs) and the reason rows refuse. |\n52|| P3-d″ producer ticked reviewer-owned checklist rows | **fixed as disposed** | The producer executed the literal instruction first and recorded the tool's refusal (`cannot hand off …: unchecked checklist items [15 16 17 18] … handoff evidence missing`), then verified each verdict row and checked it so the Change Request could construct. The handoff gate requires every item; this is the tool's contract, not a producer preference, so the disposition is correct and documented. |\n53|\n54|## Findings\n55|\n56|No P1. No P2.\n57|\n58|### P3 — measurement gaps (production correct; one member of a pinned class unmeasured)\n59|\n60|- **P3-ε `hasUnknownClass` is pinned only for the INCLUDED unknown member.** The\n61|  narrowing `if item.Class == \"unknown\" && item.Included()`\n62|  (`capturebuild.go:418`, `R6-unknown-ignores-excluded`) **SURVIVED the whole\n63|  package suite 2/2**. Under it, driven through the production entries\n64|  (`logs/probe-under-mutant-unknown-excluded.log`): `BuildCaptureManifest`\n65|  seals `raw_complete=true` for a manifest carrying an excluded unknown-class\n66|  item (spec: \"Unknown makes raw completeness false\"), `DecodeCaptureManifest`\n67|  admits `raw_complete=true` beside that item, and\n68|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` no longer blocks it — while the committed\n69|  suite (`ok`) stays green, because `TestBuildCaptureManifestUnknownMakesIncomplete`\n70|  uses an included unknown item and the shipped `N-unknown-complete` narrows\n71|  by item count, not by disposition. Production is right (my R1 probe: an\n72|  excluded unknown item seals `raw_complete=false` on the pristine tree). Fix\n73|  for the sibling: one excluded-unknown row driving build derivation, decode\n74|  and `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`, plus a harness row.\n75|- **P3-ζ the lone-surrogate member is unpinned at the shared text gate.**\n76|  `R6-text-helper-lone-title` (`validText` admits exactly one WTF-8\n77|  lone-surrogate title) **SURVIVED 2/2**: the only committed lone-surrogate row\n78|  (`capture_source_identity_native_lone_surrogate`) reaches\n79|  `SanitizeNativeKey`'s own `utf8.ValidString`, never `validText`. §1.6 names\n80|  lone surrogates explicitly and the rev4 fix scope named them; production\n81|  refuses them at every site (section T, `lone` rows). Fix: one lone-surrogate\n82|  row through a `validText` site (e.g. the title) plus a harness row.\n83|- **P3-η `EncodeNativeIdentity` standalone admits identity fields decoding\n84|  refuses.** Section T5: a 513-character native session ID or opaque identity,\n85|  kind `bogus`, and a zero `LogicalWorkspaceID` (sealed as `\"\"`) are all\n86|  encoded. Both production callers (`IdentityDigest`, `buildCaptureManifest`)\n87|  re-decode and refuse (T5-2, T5-3), and the doc comment says \"renders one\n88|  validated identity\", so no production path seals them; but the exported\n89|  entry now advertises \"encoding never admits what decoding refused\" for\n90|  extensions and native keys while still trusting the caller for bounds,\n91|  vocabulary and the workspace ID. State the pre-validated-identity bound\n92|  explicitly in TRACEABILITY.md (or re-decode inside the entry).\n93|\n94|### Informational (no action required unless cheap)\n95|\n96|- Per-member narrowings that survive because the class is pinned by another\n97|  member: `R6-sanitizer-c0-tab` (TAB; C0 pinned by U+0000/U+001F/U+007F, and\n98|  `R6-sanitizer-c0-u001f` KILLED), `R6-evidence-partial-operation` (rev4\n99|  informational re-plant; rows use `exact`). Both SURVIVED 2/2.\n100|- The sanitizer admits a single-backslash rooted key (`\\rooted`, R13) while\n101|  `\\\\unc` and `C:\\` refuse; `C:x` (drive-relative), `./x`, `%2f` and `x//y`\n102|  admit. The pinned text does not define the sanitizer's scope and the\n103|  package states its bound; Go's own `filepath.IsAbs` treats `\\rooted` as\n104|  non-absolute. Worth one line in the stated bound.\n105|- The \"custom `json.Marshaler` trusted\" bound is over-conservative: marshaled\n106|  extension bytes pass `checkExtensionsClosed` → `environ.DecodeStrictObject`,\n107|  whose frame gate refuses invalid UTF-8 and lone-surrogate escapes (T2-14/15/16).\n108|- Spec-silent behaviours re-observed and unchanged from rev4: control\n109|  characters in a title admit (C15); `-0` seals as `0`; plan keys match as a\n110|  set (D4); an actor whose parent is itself or names no actor admits\n111|  (I23/I24); `raw_refs` order is bytewise over the JCS encoding, so offsets\n112|  `10` then `9` admit (R10s) exactly as §7.8 defines \"sorted unique\";\n113|  `CheckOrdinalContiguity` checks the set, not the slice order (I16).\n114|\n115|## What is clean (verified, not read)\n116|\n117|1. **Spec fidelity, member level** — re-extracted every closed shape from the\n118|   pinned text and compared member-for-member with the code: Raw Object\n119|   Manifest (11 members) and `RawObjectEntry` (5; the prose \"and extensions\"\n120|   is overridden by the closed shape), Capture Manifest (17), Source Basis\n121|   `ax_session` (6) / `external_native` (3), `CaptureItem` (7, nine classes),\n122|   Capture Boundary `stable` (3) / `unstable_archive` (8),\n123|   `StableSnapshotProof` (9, four kinds), `NativeIdentity` (6, three kinds),\n124|   `WorkspaceBinding` (8), Canonical Session (14), `Actor` (7, three kinds),\n125|   Canonical Event (14, 26 kinds, four visibilities), `SourceEvidence` (9,\n126|   four statuses), `RawReference` (4), eight content-block types; bounds\n127|   [1..512]/[1..4096]/[1..1024]/[0..64]/[0..128]/[0..65536]/[1..1000000]/\n128|   [1..1024]/[0..9]/[1..128][0..128]/64 KiB (bytes — R10e/f/g) all match.\n129|   The rev4→rev6 production delta (`git diff 33b52bcb 7a37841`) touches only\n130|   the UTF-8 gate sites (`decode.go` walker, `identity.go` encode sanitize,\n131|   `generation.go`, `session.go`, `event.go`, `captureitem.go`,\n132|   `rawmanifest.go` one guard) — nothing else moved, so the rev3/rev4\n133|   verification of descriptor linking, exclusion and blob install stands and\n134|   was re-executed here.\n135|2. **Refusal census** (`logs/probes-rev6-refusals.log`, 150 probes): unknown\n136|   class derives `raw_complete=false` at build (included and excluded) and\n137|   `raw_complete=true`+unknown refuses at decode; included+reason,\n138|   excluded+content, excluded−reason refuse; all four always-excluded classes\n139|   refuse included at build and decode; unsorted/duplicate items and entries\n140|   refuse at build and decode; `total_bytes` disagreement, descriptor\n141|   byte-count disagreement refuse; stable without proof / `proof:null`,\n142|   pre≠post, closed_store with identity or `input_blocked=false`,\n143|   immutable_snapshot without identity refuse; unstable with `Core=false`\n144|   refuses, `Core=true` seals and `RefuseUnstableForTarget` refuses it; every\n145|   unstable member missing or falsified refuses; `excluded_classes`\n146|   extra/missing refuse; two mains / zero mains / head outside events /\n147|   duplicate events / duplicate actors / subagent without parent / main with\n148|   parent refuse at build and decode; message payload without\n149|   `content_blocks`, block type outside the vocabulary, both/neither content\n150|   arms, 65537-byte inline content refuse (65536 admits); kind/visibility\n151|   outside the vocabularies, duplicate/65 parents, synthesized coupling in\n152|   all three directions, duplicate and unsorted `raw_refs` refuse; ordinals\n153|   `[0,2]`, `[0,0]`, `[1]` refuse; `Generation.Equal(\"g1\",\"g10\")` is false;\n154|   `ParseGeneration` refuses empty and 513 characters and admits 512\n155|   characters / 1024 bytes; the sanitizer refuses `/abs`, `C:\\`, `c:/`,\n156|   `\\\\unc`, `user:pw@host`, schemed credentials, `urn:ax:` in any case, C0/C1\n157|   controls, U+200B/U+2028/U+2029/U+FEFF and a UUIDv7 form; every one of the\n158|   four sealed shapes refuses schema swap, version `1.0.1`, unknown member,\n159|   missing member, trailing data, duplicate member, bad extension key and a\n160|   `1.5` extension value.\n161|3. **Row-21 exclusion** (`logs/probes-rev6-exclusion.log`): derived from the\n162|   source list `hosttrust.ExcludedFromReplication()` (5 paths, each also as\n163|   `…/x` and `…/deep/private-key.pem`) plus every handoff class\n164|   (`.trust-stage-*`, `.custody-stage-*`, `lock-stage-*`, `.bak.<v>`,\n165|   `.pre-rollback.<v>`, `.ax-config-*`, `.ax-config-binding.`), `../escape`,\n166|   `state/../../escape`, `host-channel/./trust.json`, `host-channel//trust.json`\n167|   and an absolute form: **every one refused at all three construction paths**\n168|   (raw entry, excluded capture item, included capture item) and at both\n169|   decode paths. `TestRawManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` /\n170|   `TestCaptureManifestExcludesTrustMaterial` carry a constructor negative per\n171|   class; the package has exactly two member-key construction paths and both\n172|   call `refuseExcludedMember`. The admitted neighbours (`HOST-CHANNEL/…`,\n173|   `host-channel\\trust.json` on POSIX, `x/host-channel/…`, bare `lock`,\n174|   `…/credentials-export.json`, `trust.json.bak`) are the hosttrust matcher's\n175|   anchored STATE_DIR-relative contract, outside this leaf, unchanged since\n176|   rev3.\n177|4. **provhost bound** — `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`\n178|   PASS on the exact tree (`logs/provhost-census.log`: 225 production files, 5\n179|   session-leaf call sites, 0 elsewhere); module grep: non-test\n180|   `VerifyObjectIdentity` callers are only `internal/sessrepo` (5 sites);\n181|   `clonebundle` production calls `CalculateObjectIdentity` ×1 and\n182|   `Canonicalize` ×3; nothing imports `clonebundle`. Accept-any-claim plants\n183|   `R6-verify-claim-any`, `R6-install-claim-any` and the entry-link plant\n184|   `R6-verify-entry-link-any` KILLED 2/2; producer\n185|   `N-descriptor-claim-agreement`, `N-install-site-claim`,\n186|   `N-descriptor-id-link` KILLED 2/2.\n187|5. **Blob install** (`logs/probes-rev6-blob-determinism.log`): exact\n188|   agreement admits; size+1, other blob, other descriptor id, forged self\n189|   claim, a different descriptor of equal size, and a chunk-coverage\n190|   disagreement (owner: \"BlobChunk coverage is 15 bytes, want exactly 16\")\n191|   refuse; install exact admits, re-install with different bytes refuses\n192|   (no-replace, \"declared and staged identity differ\"), same bytes admits\n193|   (idempotent), short/long bytes and a forged claim refuse, the empty blob\n194|   installs. The package performs no durable write (no `os`/`WriteFile`\n195|   call in production files); durability is `localstore.PutBlob` with its\n196|   landed `TestPutBlobCrashBoundariesLeaveRecoverableState` and\n197|   no-replace suites, green in the four-package run — the stated purity\n198|   bound is accurate.\n199|6. **Mutation** — shipped harness reproduced in the isolated copy: **66 KILLED\n200|   + `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED, twice**, tree restored, no `__pycache__`\n201|   (`logs/mutants-producer-run{1,2}.log`, 134 per-plant logs with exits).\n202|   My battery `reviewer_mutants_rev6.py` (30 rows × 2 runs, whole-suite\n203|   killer, identical verdicts both runs, `logs/mutants-reviewer-rev6-run{1,2}.log`):\n204|   the brief's classes KILLED — `R6-excluded-set-missing-machine_auth`,\n205|   `R6-raw-subset-admits-machine_auth`, `R6-items-dup-build`,\n206|   `R6-items-dup-decode`, `R6-raw-entries-dup-decode`, `R6-sanitizer-c0-u001f`;\n207|   plus `R6-reconcile-flag-one-way`, `R6-ordinal-dup-zero`,\n208|   `R6-excluded-exact-extra`, the three claim plants and the thirteen text\n209|   plants; `C6-comment-control` SURVIVED; the four survivors are P3-ε, P3-ζ and\n210|   the two informational per-member rows above. Determinism: identical inputs\n211|   seal byte-identical objects for all four shapes, extension insertion order\n212|   and non-canonical/reordered workspace and payload bytes seal identically,\n213|   Build output is JCS-idempotent and its self digest recomputes (D1–D9).\n214|7. **Race gate** — see the next section.\n215|8. **Hygiene** — `gofmt -l` empty; `go vet` clean; `go build ./...` OK;\n216|   `go test ./internal/clonebundle ./internal/provhost ./internal/localstore\n217|   ./internal/canonicaljson -count=1` all ok (`logs/four-packages.log`);\n218|   `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 (bindings=68, clauses 49/569 — `internal/traceability` untouched, `logs/tracecheck.log`); `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree (`logs/cataloggen.log`); `git diff --check a12d1bd 7a37841` clean; `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows` builds exit 0 (`logs/cross-builds.log`); package cover 87.1% and package `-race` ok (`logs/pkg-cover.log`, `logs/pkg-race.log`);\n219|   changed paths are exactly the 24 candidate paths (README/LOGBOOK purely\n220|   additive; nothing outside `internal/clonebundle`; `internal/traceability`\n221|   untouched; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR); the CR validation log\n222|   reports `required=30 green=30 failed=0 missing=0`. README section has the\n223|   three test commands and no capability/CLI claim. LOGBOOK entry is at the\n224|   top of the newest section. All 31 matrix-named tests exist (33 in the\n225|   package); the 18-of-18 ratio and call sites check out. Sibling bounds\n226|   stated in `doc.go`, TRACEABILITY.md and results.md.\n227|\n228|## Race gate (item 7)\n229|\n230|`internal/sessquery` is untouched by this change (the candidate touches nothing outside `internal/clonebundle`, README and LOGBOOK; nothing imports `clonebundle`). The rev6 Change Request validation ran the configured suite with the landed `-timeout 25m` and is green (`required=30 green=30`; the producer's cmd05 reports `ok internal/sessquery 390.347s`). My own measurement on the pristine candidate copy (`logs/sessquery-race.log`): `go test ./internal/sessquery -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` → `ok … 315.649s`, wall 317.9 s (user 264.5 s, sys 28.5 s), exit 0, zero `DATA RACE` lines, host load 8.78 → 7.92 with other sessions' `go` and python jobs live the whole time (an idle host was not available; nothing of mine ran concurrently). Four measurements across rounds — rev2 390.6 s, rev3 347.4 s, rev4 417.4 s, rev6 315.6 s — all sit under the old 600 s default and well under the 25 m gate; the producer's earlier 665 s was under the full concurrent suite. Disposition unchanged: host-capacity artifact, not a candidate defect; the 25 m timeout on trunk (`888ae3d`) is the orchestration fix, the gate is green in this revision, and the producer's disclosure was the right disposition.\n231|\n232|## Checklist and routing\n233|\n234|Live merged checklist: every row verified true by this review and left\n235|checked. `accept_cr(TASK-260830-24z2b3, revision=6,\n236|evidence=TASK-260830-24z2b3_review-verdict-rev6.md)` routes the element to\n237|`integrating`; the three P3 rows above are recorded for the sibling leaves\n238|(`TASK-260830-2g5be6`, `TASK-260830-32ypr2`) and do not hold this leaf.","final_result":true}}}
