{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c78f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":546,"recorded_at":1780531400001087,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"call_id":"call_01a0b280015b737781d3f9bfd21e3a9d","text":"Read text file `internal/clonesnap/testdata/mutant_harness.py`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|            shutil.copy2(backup, target)\n501|    output = (run.stdout + run.stderr).strip()\n502|    if 'build failed' in output or '\\n# ' in output or output.startswith('# '):\n503|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: build broke under the patch\", output, run.returncode, elapsed\n504|    if run.returncode == 0:\n505|        verdict = \"SURVIVED\"\n506|    elif '--- FAIL' in output or 'FAIL:' in output:\n507|        verdict = \"KILLED\"\n508|    else:\n509|        return f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: exit {run.returncode} with no kill line\", output, run.returncode, elapsed\n510|    mark = \"ok\" if verdict == mutant.expect else \"MISMATCH\"\n511|    return f\"{mark}: {mutant.name}: {verdict} (want {mutant.expect}) :: {mutant.note}\", output, run.returncode, elapsed\n512|\n513|\n514|def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n515|    log_dir: Path | None = None\n516|    selected_names: list[str] = []\n517|    args = list(argv)\n518|    while args:\n519|        if args[0] == \"--log-dir\":\n520|            if len(args) < 2:\n521|                print(\"missing directory for --log-dir\")\n522|                return 2\n523|            log_dir = Path(args[1])\n524|            args = args[2:]\n525|        else:\n526|            selected_names.append(args[0])\n527|            args = args[1:]\n528|    selected = [m for m in MUTANTS if not selected_names or m.name in selected_names]\n529|    if selected_names and len(selected) != len(selected_names):\n530|        unknown = sorted(set(selected_names) - {m.name for m in selected})\n531|        print(f\"unknown mutants: {', '.join(unknown)}\")\n532|        return 2\n533|    if log_dir is not None:\n534|        log_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n535|    failures = 0\n536|    for mutant in selected:\n537|        try:\n538|            line, output, exit_code, elapsed = run_mutant(mutant)\n539|        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n540|            line, output, exit_code, elapsed = f\"ERROR: {mutant.name}: killer timed out\", \"\", -1, 0.0\n541|        print(line, flush=True)\n542|        if log_dir is not None:\n543|            (log_dir / f\"{mutant.name}.log\").write_text(\n544|                f\"# mutant={mutant.name} path={mutant.path} -run={mutant.run}\\n\"\n545|                f\"# exit={exit_code} elapsed={elapsed:.1f}s\\n\"\n546|                f\"# find={mutant.find!r}\\n# replace={mutant.replace!r}\\n---\\n{output}\\n\"\n547|            )\n548|        if not line.startswith(\"ok:\"):\n549|            failures += 1\n550|    return 1 if failures else 0\n551|\n552|\n553|if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n554|    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c791","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":547,"recorded_at":1780531400001089,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"call_id":"call_01a0b28003df70848688220eaf51d730","text":"Read text file `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Native Capture Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-2g5be6)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/clonesnap`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|The Story's FINAL leaf carries the `internal/traceability` registry\n7|bindings and re-pin; this file is the second-leaf clause record.\n8|\n9|## Why this package captures instead of clonebundle\n10|\n11|The predecessor leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture\n12|contracts: the closed manifest/boundary/blob/identity shapes, their\n13|builders and decoders. This package owns the capture OPERATION over\n14|a real on-disk provider store: the contained walk, item\n15|classification, boundary construction from measured evidence, the\n16|source-race check, the workspace checkpoint, and target admission.\n17|Every artifact emitted here is produced through the landed\n18|clonebundle builders (`BuildRawObjectManifest`,\n19|`BuildCaptureManifest`, `SanitizeNativeKey`, `CheckDigestsEqual`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`,\n21|`InstallRawBlob`, `VerifyDescriptorAgreement`,\n22|`DecodeWorkspaceBinding`, `IdentityDigest`) and re-decoded by the\n23|landed decoders before it is published or returned; no second\n24|manifest, boundary, blob, or identity model exists here.\n25|\n26|## Landed-owner reuse\n27|\n28|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n29||---|---|---|\n30|| Manifest/boundary/item/identity shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Refuse entries above |\n31|| Store containment (openat-relative Guard walk) | `internal/secprim` | every payload open via `Guard.Open` from a verified root handle; member grammar via `CheckMemberPath` |\n32|| Durable writes (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/localstore` | payload blobs via `InstallRawBlob`, manifests and receipts via `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n33|| Blob Descriptor shape and identity | `internal/canonicaljson` | `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons; never the attesting entry |\n34|| Capture class vocabulary | `internal/clonebundle` | `ValidCaptureClass` (mirrors the `sessadapter` plan vocabulary) |\n35|| String measure, digests, UUIDv7, paths | `internal/environ`, `internal/scalar` | `StringLength`, `ParseDigest`, `ParseUUIDv7`, `ParseRelativePath`, `ParseAbsolutePath` |\n36|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` for the workspace binding and the admission receipt |\n37|\n38|## Clause map\n39|\n40|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n41||---|---|---|\n42|| 13.14.1 Raw Manifest from real bytes: sorted unique entries, sanitized key, class, byte count, blob ID, descriptor ID | `Capture`, `BuildRawObjectManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureIsByteIdenticalAcrossRuns` |\n43|| 13.14.1 Capture Manifest from real evidence: basis, boundary, items, excluded classes, derived raw_complete | `Capture`, `BuildCaptureManifest` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureOptionalAbsentSealsExcluded` |\n44|| 13.14.1 CaptureItem 9-class vocabulary + included/excluded content rule | `checkPlan` via `ValidCaptureClass`, `sealAndPublish` | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureRefusesMysteryPlanClass` |\n45|| 13.14.1 always-excluded classes never included; bytes never reach blob/manifest/log/error | `excludedClass` (never opened) | `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (one fixture member per class, full-artifact scan) |\n46|| 13.14.1 unknown makes raw_complete false and blocks maximal_safe | `sealAndPublish`, `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` | `TestCaptureUnknownMakesRawIncomplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeRequiresComplete`, `TestProjectMaximalSafeAdmitsComplete`, `TestProjectStrictExactAdmitsUnknown` |\n47|| 13.14.1 stable boundary: closed proof kind, generation, equal pre/post digests, idle facts | `sealAndPublish` via `buildBoundary` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureImmutableSnapshotProof` |\n48|| 13.14.1 size equality is never proof | `checkSourceRace` via `CheckDigestsEqual` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte` (equal-size differing bytes refuse) |\n49|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive: generation, pre/post, source_not_quiescent, explicit ack, target forbidden; core-created, archive-only | `raceOutcome`, `sealAndPublish` (`Core: true`) | `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` (literal kind/reason/ack/forbidden assertions) |\n50|| 13.14.1 G2 rejects unstable | `AdmitForTarget` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestProjectRefusesUnstable`, `TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect` |\n51|| Source race detected before projection: changed byte/size, appended record, replaced file | `walkAndMeasure`, `measurePost`, `gateSourceRace` | `TestCaptureRaceChangedByte/ChangedSize/AppendedRecord/ReplacedFile/RemovedFile` |\n52|| Race gate precedes any seal or projection output | `Capture`, `CaptureAndProject` (ORDER-PIN) | `TestCaptureRaceSealsNoManifest`, `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` |\n53|| 13.14.1 WorkspaceBinding from real state: normalized cwd, sorted unique fingerprints[0..128], branch, head/index/tree | `CheckpointWorkspace` via `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` (landed) | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceSealsObservedState`, `...RelativeCwd`, `...RootCwd`, refusal rows |\n54|| 13.14.1 no member grants filesystem authority | `workspaceCwdRelative` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceRefusesEscape/DotSegments/MissingCwd/FileCwd/SymlinkRoot` |\n55|| 13.14.1 source basis ax_session / external_native | `Capture` via `buildSourceBasis` (landed) | `TestCaptureExternalNativeBasis`, `TestCaptureRefusesMixedSourceBasis/UnknownBasisKind/UnsanitizedExternalRef` |\n56|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before publishing a referencing record | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestProjectIsIdempotent`, crash test |\n57|| 10.2 logs record digest, size, media type only | `CaptureLog` (no byte parameter) | `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureExcludesSecrets` (log scan) |\n58|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor: sorted contiguous non-overlapping chunks from zero covering size; index from zero by one; empty = size zero, no chunks | `BuildBlobDescriptor` via `CalculateObjectIdentity` + `VerifyDescriptorAgreement` | `TestCaptureEmptyMemberSealsEmptyBlob`, `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember`, `TestCaptureDescriptorAgreementEndToEnd` |\n59|| 10.2 oversized blob fails with capability_unavailable before a partial manifest | `openMember` limit gate | `TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember`, `TestCaptureRefusesSparseOversizedMember`, `TestDefaultMaxSingleBytesIs128GiB` |\n60|| 7.8 fidelity profiles strict_exact\\|maximal_safe\\|compact\\|messages_only | `AdmitForTarget`, `BuildAdmissionReceipt` | `TestProjectAdmitsStableEveryProfile`, `TestProjectRefusesUnknownProfile` |\n61|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `workspaceNullableText` via `environ.StringLength` | `TestCheckpointWorkspaceMultibyteBranch` |\n62|| Containment: symlinked intermediate and FIFO refuse before any payload open, member named; no escape past the root | `openMember` via `secprim.Guard` | `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedIntermediate/TrailingSymlink/FIFO/DirectoryMember/ParentPlanKey` |\n63|| Unplanned members refuse; one item per plan candidate | `planMemberClass` | `TestCaptureRefusesUnplannedMember/PrefixSibling/RequiredMissing/DuplicatePlanKey` |\n64|\n65|## Durability\n66|\n67|This package performs durable writes only through\n68|`localstore.ObjectStore.PutBlob`: payload blobs (via the landed\n69|`InstallRawBlob`), manifest blobs, and admission receipt blobs. The\n70|landed discipline (stage, fsync, size/digest verification, atomic\n71|no-replace install, directory fsync, quarantine on mismatch) carries\n72|the crash semantics; this package adds the publish ORDER (payloads,\n73|then raw, then capture, then receipt) and the hooks that pin it.\n74|`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` kills a live capture between\n75|the raw and capture publishes and proves the replay converges with\n76|byte-identical manifests; `TestProjectIsIdempotent` proves a\n77|replayed capture verifies and reuses every blob and publishes no\n78|half-written manifest (every manifest blob re-decodes). No second\n79|write path exists in this package.\n80|\n81|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n82|\n83|- No `ax` CLI, no provider process, no network: the store is a\n84|  fixture directory. Section 7.8 capture-plan/capture/normalize\n85|  operation wiring stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package\n86|  consumes plan keys and classes, it does not speak the adapter\n87|  protocol.\n88|- The sealed stable proof carries the gate-verified pre digest for\n89|  both capture digests: the race gate proved the measured post\n90|  equal before the seal ran, so production bytes are identical to\n91|  sealing the measurement. The ordering mutants\n92|  (`N-race-order-capture`, `N-race-order-project`) prove the gate\n93|  precedes the seal; sealing the raw post measurement instead\n94|  would fail closed under a reorder and leave the ordering\n95|  unpinned.\n96|- Excluded-class bytes are never opened, so a changed byte at\n97|  equal size inside an excluded member is below the detection\n98|  floor: presence, shape, and size changes still race. Excluded\n99|  bytes cannot affect capture output, and the never-open rule is\n100|  what the leak suite proves.\n101|- Enumeration observes names through path strings; every OPEN\n102|  descends from the verified root handle through the Guard. A\n103|  sub-walk transient swap restored before the post measurement is\n104|  below the detection floor (no filesystem snapshot); any\n105|  persistent change races, and blob integrity of the read bytes is\n106|  guaranteed by the install-time verification regardless.\n107|- Optional included-class candidates absent from the store seal as\n108|  excluded rows with reason `plan_optional_absent`; required ones\n109|  refuse. Required-ness for excluded classes is inert (presence is\n110|  irrelevant to bytes that are never opened).\n111|- `MaxSingleBytes` mirrors the Section 7.8 `ResourceLimits`\n112|  per-object bound; zero selects the Section 10.2 default of\n113|  137438953472 (32768 chunks of 4194304 bytes). The sparse\n114|  oversized row pins the default end to end without reading 128\n115|  GiB.\n116|- The admission receipt (`urn:ax:internal:clonesnap-admission-receipt`\n117|  1.0.0) proves target admission and race-before-projection\n118|  ordering only. Projection planning past admission, per-kind\n119|  event payload registries, and `strict_exact`/`compact`/\n120|  `messages_only` planning semantics are the final leaf's and the\n121|  normalization sibling's.\n122|- `internal/traceability` registry bindings and digest re-pin\n123|  (Story FINAL leaf).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
