{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c913","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":740,"recorded_at":1780531400001475,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b280-a159-7a03-846e-0574f24ef311"},"task_id":"01a0b280-a159-7a03-846e-0574f24ef311","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b280-a159-7a03-846e-0574f24ef311","chunk":"Read text file `internal/clonesnap/log.go`.\n1|package clonesnap\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"fmt\"\n5|)\n6|\n7|// This file owns the capture log. Section 10.2 requires logs to\n8|// record digest, size, and media type only, never blob contents: the\n9|// only record entry takes the member key, class, digest, size,\n10|// media type, and reason — there is no parameter blob contents could\n11|// cross. The leak suite scans every emitted line for fixture secrets.\n12|\n13|// CaptureLog is one append-only capture log.\n14|type CaptureLog struct {\n15|\tlines []string\n16|}\n17|\n18|// Linef appends one formatted log line. Callers pass digests, sizes,\n19|// media types, member keys, and stable reasons only — never source\n20|// bytes.\n21|func (log *CaptureLog) Linef(format string, arguments ...any) {\n22|\tif log == nil {\n23|\t\treturn\n24|\t}\n25|\tlog.lines = append(log.lines, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\n26|}\n27|\n28|// Lines returns a copy of the recorded lines.\n29|func (log *CaptureLog) Lines() []string {\n30|\tif log == nil {\n31|\t\treturn nil\n32|\t}\n33|\treturn append([]string(nil), log.lines...)\n34|}","final_result":true}}}
