{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d19b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b27e-c8a1-7be1-9b43-e0047ff1ed44"},"sequence":1832,"recorded_at":1780531400003659,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"42a50646-ac4c-4d20-af82-db3f2b0269ba"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b289-68c3-7992-a00d-2c3fa703e63f"},"task_id":"01a0b289-68c3-7992-a00d-2c3fa703e63f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b289-68c3-7992-a00d-2c3fa703e63f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-38-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '1,20p' LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"View current LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the gate-verified pre digest for both capture digests — production bytes are identical to sealing the measurement, and the `N-race-order-capture` / `N-race-order-project` mutants prove the gate precedes the seal and the receipt (sealing the raw post measurement would fail closed under a reorder and leave the ordering unpinned). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 28 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): no `ax` CLI/provider process/network (fixture store); Section 7.8 operation wiring stays `sessadapter`; projection planning past admission is the final leaf's; excluded-byte equal-size changes are below the detection floor (never opened by design); sub-walk transient swaps restored before post-measure are below the floor (no fs snapshot). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 17 of 17 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-2g5be6_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3623,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 906,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
